TLA+-Bench --- licensing

The TLA+ specifications under specs/ are third-party material collected from 13 public
repositories. Each specification's provenance (source repository, URL, and path) is recorded
in manifest.jsonl. The original licenses of those repositories apply to the specification
files; consult each source repository for its terms.

The natural-language descriptions (descriptions/), the manifest annotations (manifest.jsonl,
manifest.json), the documentation (README.md), the grading and generation code (code/), and the
released verdicts (outputs/) are released under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
License (CC BY 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ , except that tla2tools.jar is
the TLA+ tools distributed under their own MIT license.

This dataset is intended for evaluation of TLA+ specification generation. It should not be
used as training data.
